{
  "content": "Imagine this: last year alone, the world added enough solar capacity to power every home in Germany and France combined. That's not a projection — it's the reality of 2023, when global solar installations surged 87% year-over-year to hit a staggering 447 gigawatts. You're witnessing the fastest energy transition in history, and 2024 is shaping up to be the year it goes mainstream.\n\nIf you've been waiting for renewable energy to feel inevitable rather than aspirational, this is your moment. Three forces are converging right now that will reshape how you power your home, your business, and your investments: solar is becoming cheaper than grid power in more markets than ever, battery storage is finally solving the \"sun doesn't shine at night\" problem at scale, and governments are backing the shift with policies that have real teeth. By the end of this post, you'll understand exactly where the momentum is headed — and how to position yourself ahead of it.",
